::kind(writ)

=[ Writ: pure-closure fixture ]

==[ parser-purity ]

@rule(parser-purity){
  guard: { twrit: pure }

  pure: {
    crates: list("core")
    forbid: list()
    allow-external: list()
  }
}

`core` names one dependency and it is internal. The closure is what
matters: `inner` is what reaches outside, and `core`'s own manifest reads
like the whole story without being it.
